{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc | sed -n '85,165p;325,405p;635,675p;735,825p'\"","aggregated_output":"    85\t   :register \"DebruijnRegisterVM\"})\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\t(defn- packet->named-datoms\n    89\t  \"The named `:yin/*` datoms of one expanded tree packet, the input the de\n    90\t   Bruijn resolver reads.\"\n    91\t  [packet]\n    92\t  (vm/ast->datoms\n    93\t    (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast (macro/packet->row-set packet))))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn- relocate\n    97\t  \"Shift every `:pc`-kind operand of `inst`, per `opcode-table`, by\n    98\t   `offset`.\"\n    99\t  [opcode-table offset inst]\n   100\t  (reduce (fn [inst [i [_ kind]]]\n   101\t            (if (= :pc kind) (update inst (inc i) + offset) inst))\n   102\t          inst\n   103\t          (map-indexed vector (get opcode-table (nth inst 0)))))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn- chain-hash\n   107\t  \"The identity of a held image extended by one segment.  Callers pass a\n   108\t   nil `held-hash` for an empty held image, whatever `:hash` the fresh VM\n   109\t   carries, so the first link is the segment's own identity.\n   110\t\n   111\t   Invariant: a de Bruijn VM this shell loads carries, as `:hash`, a hash\n   112\t   chain over its segments in load order: the first segment's own H (or\n   113\t   R), then `sha256(previous || H(segment))` for each later segment.\n   114\t   Relocation is a function of the held image's length, which the previous\n   115\t   link already fixes, so the chain names the concatenated image as\n   116\t   uniquely as H over it would, yet each load hashes only its new segment.\n   117\t   After the first input it differs from H over the concatenation; a\n   118\t   continuation stamped under one link is refused after the next load,\n   119\t   exactly as a whole-image H refused it.\"\n   120\t  [held-hash segment-hash]\n   121\t  (if held-hash (jing/sha256 (str held-hash segment-hash)) segment-hash))\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\t(defn- append-stack-image\n   125\t  \"Load `image` after the stack image `vm` already holds and start at its\n   126\t   first instruction.  A closure a previous input stored (a `def`) names a\n   127\t   body pc in the earlier image, so that image is kept, not replaced.\n   128\t   `load-image` sees the new segment alone, so H is computed over it only\n   129\t   and folded into the held identity by `chain-hash`.\"\n   130\t  [vm image]\n   131\t  (let [held (:segment vm)\n   132\t        offset (count held)\n   133\t        shift #(relocate dcode/opcode-table offset %)\n   134\t        loaded (stack/load-image vm image)]\n   135\t    (assoc loaded\n   136\t           :segment (into held (map shift) image)\n   137\t           :hash (chain-hash (when (pos? offset) (:hash vm)) (:hash loaded))\n   138\t           :pc offset)))\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn- append-register-image\n   142\t  \"The register image counterpart of `append-stack-image`.  The incoming\n   143\t   image is validated and hashed alone by `load-image`, which also sizes\n   144\t   the register file for its main body; the image it runs in is the\n   145\t   concatenation, whose later main bodies end in `:halt` as the first\n   146\t   does, and its identity is the `chain-hash` link.\"\n   147\t  [vm {:keys [bodies instructions] :as image}]\n   148\t  (let [held (:segment vm)\n   149\t        offset (count (:instructions held))\n   150\t        shift-body #(-> % (update :start + offset) (update :end + offset))\n   151\t        shift #(relocate rcode/opcode-table offset %)\n   152\t        loaded (register/load-image vm image)]\n   153\t    (assoc loaded\n   154\t           :segment {:bodies (into (:bodies held) (map shift-body) bodies)\n   155\t                     :instructions (into (:instructions held)\n   156\t                                         (map shift)\n   157\t                                         instructions)}\n   158\t           :hash (chain-hash (when (pos? offset) (:hash vm)) (:hash loaded))\n   159\t           :pc offset)))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(def program-loaders\n   163\t  \"The loader the evaluator observer hands each `program-out` value, per\n   164\t   evaluator.  Every value there is one expanded canonical tree packet\n   165\t   `[root rows]` (yin.vm.macro.md §2.4); each loader takes its row set — the\n   325\t  (assoc-in state [:ledger medium] outcome))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn drain-output\n   329\t  \"Drain the output medium into `[state text results]`, total over every\n   330\t   `next` outcome.  `results` holds, in order, every `:repl/result` token\n   331\t   read, unchanged; every other element is printed text.\n   332\t\n   333\t   `ok` advances to the exact successor the handle returned and spends one\n   334\t   of `drain-budget` element reads.  `gap` prints a loss notice, resumes at\n   335\t   the recovery cursor, and spends one of `gap-budget` instead, so a gap\n   336\t   never starves the drain of an element it must still reach.  `end`,\n   337\t   `cursor-mismatch`, `invalid-cursor`, and `transport-error` print a\n   338\t   notice, leave the cursor unchanged, and end the drain.  Whatever ended the\n   339\t   drain is recorded in the ledger, so `repl-state` never has to ask a stream\n   340\t   how it is.\"\n   341\t  [state]\n   342\t  (let [output (:output-stream state)\n   343\t        cursor (:output-cursor state)]\n   344\t    (cond\n   345\t      (nil? output) [(ledger state :output :untried) \"\" []]\n   346\t      (nil? cursor) [(ledger state :output :dao.stream/invalid-cursor)\n   347\t                     \";; output unreadable: no cursor was minted\\n\"\n   348\t                     []]\n   349\t      :else\n   350\t      (loop [remaining drain-budget\n   351\t             gaps gap-budget\n   352\t             cursor cursor\n   353\t             chunks []\n   354\t             results []]\n   355\t        (if (or (zero? remaining) (zero? gaps))\n   356\t          [(-> state\n   357\t               (assoc :output-cursor cursor)\n   358\t               (ledger :output :dao.stream/blocked))\n   359\t           (apply str chunks)\n   360\t           results]\n   361\t          (let [result (stream/next output cursor)\n   362\t                outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   363\t                value (:dao.stream/value result)]\n   364\t            (case outcome\n   365\t              :dao.stream/ok\n   366\t              (if (result-chunk? value)\n   367\t                (recur (dec remaining)\n   368\t                       gaps\n   369\t                       (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n   370\t                       chunks\n   371\t                       (conj results value))\n   372\t                (recur (dec remaining)\n   373\t                       gaps\n   374\t                       (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n   375\t                       (conj chunks (chunk-text value))\n   376\t                       results))\n   377\t\n   378\t              :dao.stream/gap\n   379\t              (recur remaining\n   380\t                     (dec gaps)\n   381\t                     (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n   382\t                     (conj chunks\n   383\t                           (str \";; output lost: resumed at the recovery\"\n   384\t                                \" cursor\\n\"))\n   385\t                     results)\n   386\t\n   387\t              :dao.stream/blocked\n   388\t              [(-> state\n   389\t                   (assoc :output-cursor cursor)\n   390\t                   (ledger :output outcome))\n   391\t               (apply str chunks)\n   392\t               results]\n   393\t\n   394\t              [(-> state\n   395\t                   (assoc :output-cursor cursor)\n   396\t                   (ledger :output outcome))\n   397\t               (apply str (conj chunks (str \";; output \" (name outcome) \"\\n\")))\n   398\t               results])))))))\n   399\t\n   400\t\n   401\t(defn- make-output-medium!\n   402\t  []\n   403\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n   404\t    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n   405\t                   ring/capacity-key output-capacity})))\n   635\t         :last-value-2 (:last-value state)\n   636\t         :last-value-3 (:last-value-2 state)))\n   637\t\n   638\t\n   639\t(defn- round-id\n   640\t  \"The identity of the state's current round: the shell's token, minted\n   641\t   once per shell value, with its round count.  A medium the caller\n   642\t   supplies may already hold results from another shell or an earlier\n   643\t   round; none of them carries this identity.\"\n   644\t  [state]\n   645\t  [(:shell-token state) (:round state)])\n   646\t\n   647\t\n   648\t(defn- finalize-eval\n   649\t  \"Drain the round's output and its result from the output medium.  Only a\n   650\t   result stamped with this round's identity is this round's value; the\n   651\t   evaluator answers once per halted program, after its prints.  A missing\n   652\t   or foreign-round result is loss, reported with the append outcome the\n   653\t   runner recorded.\"\n   654\t  [state state' vm']\n   655\t  (let [append (::result-append vm')\n   656\t        [state'' output-text results]\n   657\t        (drain-output (assoc state' :vm (dissoc vm' ::result-append)))\n   658\t        round (round-id state')\n   659\t        current (filterv #(= round (:round %)) results)]\n   660\t    (if (seq current)\n   661\t      (let [value (:value (peek current))]\n   662\t        [(record-last-value state state'' value)\n   663\t         (str output-text (format-value value))])\n   664\t      [state''\n   665\t       (str output-text \"Error: \" result-loss-text\n   666\t            (when (and append (not= :dao.stream/ok append))\n   667\t              (str \" (append: \" (name append) \")\")))])))\n   668\t\n   669\t\n   670\t(defn- drain-observer\n   671\t  \"Advance one observer past every batch still on its medium, keeping any\n   672\t   gap it recovers across.  A nil observer — a session without that medium —\n   673\t   stays nil.\"\n   674\t  [observer]\n   675\t  (when observer\n   735\t  \"Drive the evaluator's observer over `program-out`: it loads each\n   736\t   expanded tree packet into the VM, runs it, and answers its value on the\n   737\t   output medium.  The two stages meet only at `program-out`; neither calls\n   738\t   the other.\"\n   739\t  [{:keys [load-program output-stream] :as state}]\n   740\t  (let [{:keys [observer] vm :consumer}\n   741\t        (observer/run-on-stream {:observer (:row-observer state),\n   742\t                                 :consumer (:vm state)}\n   743\t                                engine/ready-for-ingress?\n   744\t                                load-program\n   745\t                                (make-runner output-stream (round-id state)))]\n   746\t    (assoc state :row-observer observer :vm vm)))\n   747\t\n   748\t\n   749\t(defn- format-expansion-errors\n   750\t  [errors]\n   751\t  (str/join \"\\n\" (map #(str \"Error: Macro expansion failed: \" (format-value %))\n   752\t                      errors)))\n   753\t\n   754\t\n   755\t(defn- run-evaluation\n   756\t  \"The evaluator half of a round whose expander forwarded a program: run\n   757\t   it, then either finalize the value or consume the failure.  `state` is\n   758\t   the round's starting state; `expanded` already carries the expander's\n   759\t   progress, which a failing evaluation keeps.\"\n   760\t  [state expanded]\n   761\t  (try\n   762\t    (let [gaps-before (ingress-gaps expanded)\n   763\t          evaluated (run-evaluator-stage expanded)]\n   764\t      (cond\n   765\t        (> (ingress-gaps evaluated) gaps-before)\n   766\t        [(assoc evaluated :ingress-loss? true)\n   767\t         (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n   768\t\n   769\t        (vm/halted? (:vm evaluated))\n   770\t        (finalize-eval state evaluated\n   771\t                       (engine/restore-initial-env (:env (:vm expanded))\n   772\t                                                   (:vm evaluated)))\n   773\t\n   774\t        :else\n   775\t        (throw\n   776\t          (ex-info\n   777\t            \"Program stream did not form a complete, runnable Yin VM program.\n   778\tHint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n   779\t            {:vm-type (:vm-type state)}))))\n   780\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n   781\t      (consume-failed-round (assoc expanded :vm (:vm state)) error))))\n   782\t\n   783\t\n   784\t(defn- eval-program\n   785\t  \"Evaluate one frontend program — the map AST the compilers emit or a\n   786\t   datom-literal program — through the §10.1 composition.  The encoder\n   787\t   projects it to an input batch of canonical rows with its harvest and\n   788\t   declaration rows; the shell appends that batch to `program-in`, drives\n   789\t   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the evaluator only when a\n   790\t   program was forwarded.  An expansion failure is reported as data: its\n   791\t   batch is consumed, the store keeps its previous macros, and the next\n   792\t   input evaluates normally.  An encoding failure throws before anything\n   793\t   is appended.\n   794\t\n   795\t   The observers recover across a gap on their own, but the shell reads the\n   796\t   gap counts around the round: an increase on any medium means one or more\n   797\t   batches were never run, so resuming as though execution were complete\n   798\t   would report a result built on programs the VM never saw.  The loss is\n   799\t   reported and the shell refuses further evaluation until `(reset)`.\n   800\t\n   801\t   A completed program's lexical environment does not outlive it: the VM's\n   802\t   environment is restored to the one the round began with, as `vm/eval`\n   803\t   does.  A round that throws is consumed by `consume-failed-round`.\"\n   804\t  [state program]\n   805\t  (if (:ingress-loss? state)\n   806\t    [state (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n   807\t    (let [state' (update (inject-last-value state) :round inc)\n   808\t          batch (encoder/program-batch program)\n   809\t          append (stream/append! (:program-stream state') batch)]\n   810\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome append))\n   811\t        [state (str \"Error: program batch not ingested: \"\n   812\t                    (name (:dao.stream/outcome append)))]\n   813\t        (let [expanded (try\n   814\t                         (run-expander-stage state')\n   815\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   816\t                                   :clj Exception\n   817\t                                   :cljs js/Error) error\n   818\t                           {:failed (consume-failed-round state error)}))]\n   819\t          (if-let [failed (:failed expanded)]\n   820\t            failed\n   821\t            (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded]\n   822\t              (cond\n   823\t                (> (ingress-gaps expanded) (ingress-gaps state'))\n   824\t                [(assoc expanded :ingress-loss? true)\n   825\t                 (str \"Error: \" ingress-loss-text)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
